    "body": "Coding agent review loops matters because the mechanism behind the trend is starting to affect real product design. The right reader question is not whether the topic is popular, but what must be true before a team can connect automated coding to engineering quality gates.\n\n## The mechanism\n\nMost AI shifts become business-relevant only after three things line up: a reliable model capability, a workflow where the output can be checked and a distribution path that puts the feature in front of real users. Coding agent review loops is useful to watch because it sits at that intersection.\n\n## Evidence to read first\n\n- OpenAI: Building self-improving tax agents with Codex\n- OpenAI: OpenAI News\n- Vercel: Vercel Blog\n- Anthropic: Anthropic Research\n\n## A practical model\n\n| Lens | Useful question | Editorial output |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Market | What actually changed around Coding agent review loops? | Separate source facts from interpretation. |\n| Reader | What decision does the operator need to make? | Give a direct answer before analysis. |\n| Risk | What could be wrong or early? | Mark uncertainty and avoid fake precision. |\n| Action | What is the smallest next step? | Translate the signal into how to connect automated coding to engineering quality gates. |\n\n:::chart\ntitle: Coding agent review loops signal radar\nlabels: Source confidence|Market heat|Workflow impact|Execution difficulty\nvalues: 74|79|57|68\ncaption: Relative editorial scores for framing the article, not market sizing or investment advice.\n:::\n\n## Limits\n\nThe strongest writing in AI is comfortable saying what is not proven yet. For Coding agent review loops, the limits are source freshness, measurement quality and operational ownership. Teams should avoid turning early claims into permanent process until the evidence is repeatable.\n\n## ALTOS LAB editorial note\n\nOur read: this is not just a trend page. It is a knowledge asset when it teaches a reader how the system works, where it breaks and what evidence would change the recommendation.",
